  PASS  L1b with c added: an M-free group containing a0 exists (kappa itself)
  variables ['G', 'rho', 'M', 'a0', 'muK'] -> 2 dimensionless group(s)
    exponents {'G': '-1', 'rho': '-2/3', 'M': '-1/3', 'a0': '1', 'muK': '0'}
    exponents {'G': '0', 'rho': '-1/3', 'M': '1/3', 'a0': '0', 'muK': '1'}
  with the clock mass mu_K (a length^-1) instead of c: a0 mu_K/(G rho) is M-free; mu_K is bounded and free
  (galaxy bound <= 0.1/Mpc, CMB wants >= 198/Mpc; MK1 NO VALUE), so that group is a TRADE, not a kappa.
  Which new inputs carry c? COL1 (weak-field collapse in an FRW background, units kpc, km/s, Msun; c absent),
  FLD1 (reads COL1-type runs), FB1 identities (sigma^2 = (1/2) sqrt(G M a0), J(g) = (a0^2/K)[u - ln(1+u)]): none.
  Radii and times in them are set by (G, rho, M_b): R ~ (M/rho)^(1/3), t ~ 1/sqrt(G rho), which reduces to base.

